    "title": "Ratliff notches 200th career win - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Steve LeMaster Sports Writer ,\n9 hours ago HAZARD — Perry Central head coach Bobby Ratliff notched his 200th career win during the 2026 high school softball season. Ratliff reached the coaching milestone in May. Among the top active high school softball coaches in Eastern Kentucky, Ratliff guided Perry Central to 26 wins during its latest campaign. The Lady Commodores compiled a 26-14 record in the 2026 high school softball season. Under the direction of Ratliff, Perry Central captured the 54th District title and reached the semifinals of the 14th Region Softball Tournament. Read full article",
